s5p-mfc: let the client hold more decoded frames than five.

A decoder's capture queue was capped at the DPB the firmware asks for plus
five. FFmpeg's V4L2 decoder (mpv, through it) holds several decoded frames of
its own: while the display is not taking frames for a moment (an app's page
turning), those five ran out, the firmware had nowhere to decode into and
stopped taking stream buffers, and FFmpeg waited for a free one in poll()
with no timeout, so mpv's core, and every app call into mpv, hung for good.
Allow sixteen. The buffers come from CMA (256 MB on the Galaxy M20).

45:#define MFC_MAX_EXTRA_DPB       16
--- a/drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc_common.h
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc_common.h
@@ -42,7 +42,7 @@
 #include <media/videobuf2-dma-contig.h>
 
 /* MFC definitions */
-#define MFC_MAX_EXTRA_DPB       5
+#define MFC_MAX_EXTRA_DPB       16
 #define MFC_MAX_BUFFERS		32
 #define MFC_NUM_CONTEXTS	4
 /* Interrupt timeout */
